# Project: ResearchFlow (Multi-Agent Research & Report Generator)

Users enter a research topic, review an AI-generated plan, approve it, then watch a
live multi-agent style run that writes and verifies a report section by section.

Current phase is frontend-focused AI integration inside Next.js. Do not build a
separate backend yet.

## Current stack (do not substitute in this phase)

- App: Next.js 15 App Router + React 19 + TypeScript
- UI: existing ResearchFlow components, Tailwind, Motion, Lucide
- State: React Context (`ResearchContext`) — do not add Redux/Zustand unless asked
- AI: OpenRouter via `@openrouter/sdk`, called only from Next.js route handlers
- Secrets: `.env.local` server vars only (`OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, `OPENROUTER_MODEL`)
- Never use `NEXT_PUBLIC_OPENROUTER_API_KEY` or call OpenRouter from client components

## Hard exclusions for this phase

Do not add: FastAPI, LangGraph, CrewAI, Supabase, Redis, Celery/workers, Prisma,
PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or a separate backend service.

## Folder structure (current)

```
researchflow/src/
  app/                 Next.js pages + api/ai/* route handlers
  components/          UI by feature (landing, research, plan, live, report)
  context/             ResearchContext state
  lib/ai/              openrouter, prompts, helpers, mappers, client, logger
  mocks/               mock sources/events/cost/history (keep hybrid)
  types/               domain + AI types
```

## AI architecture rules

1. All OpenRouter calls go through `src/lib/ai/openrouter.ts`.
2. Prompts live in `src/lib/ai/prompts.ts` — not inline in React components.
3. API routes under `src/app/api/ai/` validate input, call AI helpers, return JSON.
4. Structured AI output must be validated before returning to the client.
5. Every AI call should be logged (model, latency, success/failure, short preview).
6. Live run: real AI for research/plan/improve/write/verify (sources, findings, timeline, tokens/cost from OpenRouter). Instant Demo / history seeds may still use mocks.

## Product rules

- Preserve existing UI design, routes, colors, typography, and layouts.
- Prefer editing existing files over creating parallel `*_new` / `*_v2` files.
- Loading, empty, and error states for every AI-backed action.
- Never expose API keys, raw provider errors, or secrets to the browser.
- Do not stub with `TODO` unless explicitly asked. Ship working code.

## Working style

- When a task spans multiple files, list files you will touch before coding.
- Types first, then implementation.
- After finishing, state what acceptance criteria were satisfied.
